From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -write_priority or, colliding writes
 OR'd
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-write_priority says what a word takes when two write ports write it in
one cycle: last, the last port's data, as before; or or, the OR of every
writing port's data. firtool's register files (XiangShan's IntRegFile,
FpRegFile, VfRegFile) merge their writes with an OR, so a generated
register file in their place is equivalent to the RTL only with or; it
also drops each word's priority logic, an inverter and an AND2 per port
but the last. The behavioral model follows the option.

The fourteenth of the generate_regfile features carried onto
generate_ram (generate_regfile's default); see OpenROAD #11669. Not
upstreamed.

Tested: src/ram/test/write_priority_or_asap7.tcl.

Commit 14 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
